{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E3TM7HA5Qd49PWApZBeLBi","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on the context filesystem, **destination-created mirror topics use the destination cluster's default replication factor** — they do not inherit the source topic's replication factor by default.\\\\n\\\\nThis is explicitly stated in the KIP-1279 (Cluster Mirroring) design discussion:\\\\n\\\\nIn the response to comment AS25, Federico Valeri (KIP author) clarifies:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"Anyway, we decided to remove the --replication-factor flag to always honor the destination cluster default. The operator can always use the assignment script to change it.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThe original concern, raised by Andrew Schofield, noted that while source and mirror topics might intentionally have different replication factors, the default behavior is to use the **destination cluster's default replication factor** rather than copying the source topic's replication factor.\\\\n\\\\n**Files cited:**\\\\n- `/store/kips/KIP-1279/2026-04-15-discuss-cluster-mirroring-d1515ee7.md` (lines 28-31) - Federico Valeri's response confirming the design decision\\\\n- `/store/mail/2026-04-03-mail-3da03c7762b02a3dc6d931ae-3cd2d5a4.md` (line 67) - Andrew Schofield's original question about this behavior\\\\n- `/store/kips/KIP-1279/2026-04-07-mail-9733e74f5415b581f89213be-756d0d01.md` (line 83) - Same question in another email thread\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1279/2026-04-07-mail-9733e74f5415b581f89213be-756d0d01.md\\\",\\\"mail/2026-04-03-mail-3da03c7762b02a3dc6d931ae-3cd2d5a4.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1279/2026-04-15-discuss-cluster-mirroring-d1515ee7.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":32.51,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":1,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":177921,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":40353,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.1097271,\\\"input_tokens\\\":74,\\\"output_tokens\\\":2231}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_